@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] nav-back-returns-to-the-exact-place
After following a link out of a page (a tour's source, a mention, a file, a path), Back
MUST return to that page scrolled exactly where it was, with what was open still open.
For a mention in an Ask answer that place is the Ask sheet at the same scroll. Tavi on
0.31.0: "I go back, I am still here. Great. This is what we wanted ... I hope that's in a
contract, because it's very important" (recording 15 Oct 13:54, 07:03 to 07:15; K15;
J35; rule 123).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-back-keeps-the-page-state
A page under another page keeps its state while the other is on top: its scroll, its open
folds, its selected tab and anything typed. Opening something from a page and coming back
MUST NOT rebuild it from the top (recording 14 Oct 19:19, 04:15 to 04:47; rule 123).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] nav-back-always-goes-backward
Back, the phone's Back and a back swipe always move toward the page before, whichever
page they land on; a back swipe moves the page with the finger and carries it on that
way (rule 105).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] nav-pages-slide
Opening a page (a pull request from a row, by tap or by swipe, a repository) and
returning slide the page in from the side it belongs to; nothing pops. The stack of pages
is ranked by depth (rules 88 and 105; F7).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-one-destination-one-presentation
A destination reached from more than one place opens the same way from each: always as a
sheet or always as a page, never a sheet from one place and a page from another (rule 66).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-pull-down-for-commands-everywhere
Pulling any page's list down past its top opens Commands: the Inbox, Tours, a repository's
lists, and the Overview, Diff and Tour of a pull request, with "Pull for commands" then
"Release for commands" while pulling ("I should be able to pull for commands on any page.
Again, consistency", rule 117; J30; F4).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] nav-commands-is-a-bottom-sheet
Commands is a bottom sheet like any other: it rises from the bottom and a throw down
carries it on down. It MUST NOT drop in from the top (H6; rules 105 and 108).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-commands-ready-to-type
Commands opens at its tall height and its search takes the keyboard as the sheet rises,
not after it rests, so a command can be typed at once, and it opens without a delay after the pull (J11;
recording 15 Oct 13:54, 00:56 to 01:05; K5; rule 77).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-commands-reach-everywhere
Commands holds Home, Settings, the theme, Update Pully, What's new and Send feedback on
every page, and a page adds its own commands while it is open. Commands is the one palette: there is no
second command menu and no Commands row in the ⋯ or profile sheets (rules 61 and 104;
J30, H22; recording 15 Oct 13:54, 12:33).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-commands-themes
Commands offers Themes, which opens the same theme sheet as Settings (recording 15 Oct
13:54, 08:33 to 09:11; K18).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-commands-follow-the-page
Commands leads with a Suggested group, the actions of the page on screen: on the Tour, Ask
about this tour, Switch to the diff, Regenerate tour and the next and previous stop; on a
pull request's Overview, Review files, Ask, Leave a comment and Approve; on the Diff, the
next and previous file, Mark reviewed and Find a file. The other groups follow, and General
is always last (circled General, recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 08:31 to 09:04, N14).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] nav-link-closes-what-was-open
A pull request link that arrives (shared to Pully or tapped in another app) first sends any
open sheet down the way a sheet closes and closes Settings, then opens the pull request, so
going back finds the Inbox with nothing left open (recording 16 Oct 13:06, 00:35 to 01:20 and 02:41 to 02:44;
O1, O4, rule 175).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-back-asks-before-closing
Back on the Inbox MUST NOT close Pully at once: it asks "Close Pully?" with Close Pully and
Stay (recording 16 Oct 13:06, 02:47 to 02:55; O5, rule 176).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-feedback-from-anywhere
Send feedback is in Commands on every page and is a row of Settings, and both open the same
page: one note, a quiet line with the version, the phone and the screen it goes with, and
Send feedback, then the account's last notes with Done on those an agent has acted on.
From Commands it is a sheet of its own over the page, from Settings a page inside the
Settings sheet, as the theme list is (nav-commands-themes). The note goes to the server
with the screen and the pull request or repository of the page it was opened over, and
what was typed MUST outlive closing the sheet and a send that fails ("Let's add a button
somewhere for me to leave feedback from the app itself": Tavi, 20 Oct 2026 06:10).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-on-github-leaves-pully
Every action that says GitHub (the ⋯ sheet's GitHub tile, Open on GitHub, a comment's age,
"more on GitHub", a check's row) MUST open the page outside Pully: the GitHub app when it
takes the page, otherwise the phone's browser. It MUST NOT go through the link filter that
hands github.com pull request links to Pully, which took the link back so nothing happened
("the GitHub link in the bottom sheet doesn't open GitHub because Pully grabs it so nothing
happens. That needs fixing": Tavi, 20 Oct 2026 12:10).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] nav-links-inside-open-like-outside
A link tapped inside Pully, in a description, a comment or an answer, opens in Pully exactly
when a tap on it in another app would (a GitHub pull request, commit or compare link, on the
thing it points at, pr-links-land-on-the-thing, or a page of Pully's own server that Pully has a
screen for), and outside Pully otherwise.
